# Build context for backend/Dockerfile is the repo root (the npm workspace
# lockfile lives there). BuildKit reads this file instead of /.dockerignore
# when building with `-f backend/Dockerfile`. Allowlist: only what the image
# needs, so web/ edits, .env files and node_modules never reach the builder.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!web/package.json
!backend/package.json
!backend/tsconfig.json
!backend/src
!deploy/backend
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
